From 7f5186346eccf63ea7b4ebcd3f623756bc3c0129 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jgsuess <782737+jgsuess@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 10:30:25 +1000
Subject: [PATCH] frontend: ClusterTable: Fix registerClusterStatus
 fall-through

ClusterStatus rendered each registered status callback as a JSX element
and treated a null result as "not handled". A JSX element is never null,
so the first registered callback always won: when it rendered null (as
the minikube plugin does for non-minikube clusters), the Status cell
stayed empty and later callbacks and the default status never showed.

Each callback now runs in its own small component, called as a
function so that null or undefined falls through to the next callback
and finally to the default status. Running each callback in its own
component instance, keyed by the callback's identity rather than its
position, keeps hooks inside callbacks valid across re-renders and
when plugins register more callbacks, so existing plugins whose status
component uses hooks keep working. Calling the callbacks directly from
ClusterStatus would attach their hooks to ClusterStatus and crash it on
the next render.

A callback that throws is caught by the existing ErrorBoundary and the
next callback is tried, so one broken plugin does not blank the cell.

The rest of the chain is passed on as a single element and expanded
only when a link falls through or throws, so a render builds one link
per callback tried rather than the whole remaining chain at every link.

The registerClusterStatus docs now describe the fall-through contract.
The section in docs/development/api/modules/plugin_registry.md is
written by hand: running TypeDoc rewrites the whole generated tree in a
newer layout.
